Coronavirus 2 associated with severe acute respiratory syndrome (SARS-CoV-2) is an emerging coronavirus associated with severe acute respiratory syndrome (ACRS), where it was first isolated from three people with pneumonia in the group of cases of acute respiratory disease in Wuhan.
SARS-CoV-2 is involved in its characteristics with relevant coronaviruses found in nature.
