Covid-19 in the most rapidly affected may develop acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS), resulting in respiratory failure, septic shock or multi-organ failure.
Complications associated with COVID-19 are sepsis, abnormal blood clots, and damage to the heart, kidneys and liver.
