Cytokine storm may be a complication in the later stages of acute COVID-19.
There is evidence that hydroxychloroquine may have anti-cytokine storm properties. China's National Health Communiqué Tosilizumab has added to treatment guidelines after completing a small study.
He is undergoing a non-random stage 2 test at the national level in Italy after showing positive results in those with severe medical conditions.
